  "worked_solution": "Remember that the eigenvectors of $A$ are the non-zero vectors $v$ such that $Av=\\lambda v.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Av & =\\lambda v \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2c\\end{aligned}] & =3[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2c\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}1-4c \\\\ -2+8c\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 6c\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}1-4c=-3 \\\\ -2+8c=6c\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Solving for $c$ in the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n1-4c=-3\\,\u27f9\\,c=1.\n$$\n\n- Solving for $c$ in the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n-2+8c=6c\\,\u27f9\\,c=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution of the system is $c=1.$",
